  "description": "**Class-BARS (Biometric Attendance Recording System)** is a web application for recording student class attendance using facial recognition. Lecturers start a session for a course/venue; enrolled students check in by looking at their camera — a face embedding is matched against the student's stored template and attendance is recorded. Check-in also verifies the student is near the session venue using a PostGIS geofence (a circle or a four-corner class box); only the gap from the fence and reported GPS accuracy are stored, never raw coordinates. OTP fallback is still deferred.",
